  "difficulty_reason": "Supplying the named Lagrangian-minimizer framework and the small-noise-zone decoupling leaves a source-local construction that must work simultaneously for every mean theta on one realization of the forcing. The proof extends an interval minimizer backwards through the regeneration times t_k=T_*(t_{k-1}), shows that the intervals tile (-infinity,t], transfers the action additively along the chain, and then obtains extremal elements from finiteness of the interval minimizer sets together with path surgery. The retained core is where the mechanism lives: the explicit 1/(4M) strength comparison of Proposition 2.2 and the T_* finiteness argument of Proposition 2.4, so nothing is assumed that the source does not prove. This is the existence theorem that the introduction states as Theorem 1.4, and it is above ordinary PhD qualification problems in stochastic homogenization or the calculus of variations.",
